## Conventions that differ from defaults

<!--
  Only things that would surprise a competent stranger.

  A style rule that is true of EVERY project belongs in
  %USERPROFILE%\.claude\CLAUDE.md, not here - see 04-file-conventions.md
  section 6. Repeat it here only when the repo is public or shared, so a
  collaborator who does not have your user-level file still sees it.
-->
- **ASCII only** in prose, code, comments, and filenames: `-` not em/en dashes,
  `->` not arrows, `...` not an ellipsis character, straight quotes. Exception:
  genuine data (author names, dataset titles, recorded API responses) keeps
  whatever characters it actually contains.
- <e.g. "Sidecar JSON is written with 2-space indent and sorted keys; downstream diffs depend on it.">
- <e.g. "Column order in events.tsv is significant - never reorder.">

## Gotchas

<!-- Non-obvious behaviour that has bitten you before. -->
- <e.g. "The citation cache is keyed by DOI, not dataset ID. Two datasets can share a citation.">

## Where the thinking lives

- `.status/decisions.md` - decisions and their rationale. **Read this before
  proposing structural changes.** Append entries; never rewrite existing ones.
- `.status/*-plan.md` - active plans with `[ ] TODO` / `[x] DONE` markers.
  Check the markers before starting work.

## Working agreements

<!-- Behavioural rules. Emphasis words genuinely improve adherence. -->
- IMPORTANT: Never edit or delete files under `.status/` without asking first.
- For changes spanning more than 3 files, write a plan to `.status/` and stop for review.
- When you are guessing about an external API or data format, say so explicitly
  rather than assuming.
- Show evidence, not assertions: the command you ran and its output.

